ADDITIONAL ENGAGEMENT-SPECIFIC NOTICE (not a licence condition; please read)

This repository documents a penetration testing engagement conducted under
written authorization for Networkwalks internship batch B083. Two categories of
material are deliberately EXCLUDED from this repository and are governed by
separate, stricter handling rules rather than by this open-source licence:

  1. CLIENT CONFIDENTIAL MATERIAL. Milestone detail, verified finding write-ups,
     unredacted evidence, and client-supplied artefacts remain client
     confidential. Their handling is governed by the engagement authorization and
     rules of engagement, NOT by the MIT licence above. Publishing this
     repository does not waive those confidentiality obligations.

  2. CLIENT-SENSITIVE DATA. No patient records, medical data, employee salary
     figures, shareholder personal details, credentials, tokens, session
     material or private keys are present in this repository, by design. The
     patterns that would match such data are listed in .gitignore so that they
     are blocked from being committed.

Because the above material is excluded, the MIT licence applies only to the
documentation, diagrams, templates and scripts authored for this repository.

SYNTHETIC EXAMPLE DATA. All example content is machine-generated and labelled
"SYNTHETIC - NOT CLIENT DATA". It contains no real person, system, patient,
employee, shareholder or credential. Any resemblance to real data is
coincidental.

THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL. Tool names referenced in the documentation remain the
property of their respective owners and are used for identification only.

NETWORKWALKS AND CLIENT NAME. Networkwalks and the client organisation are the
property of their respective owners. This repository is an individual intern
portfolio artefact. It is not an official, reviewed, or endorsed publication of
Networkwalks or of the client, and no claim of client approval of its contents
is made or implied.
